==English==
{{wikipedia|Silver Jubilee}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[silver anniversary]] of a [[coronation]], the [[25]][[-th|th]] [[anniversary]] of a [[monarch]]'s [[rule]].
# {{lb|en|uncommon}} {{synonym of|en|silver anniversary}} ''[[more]] [[generally]]''.
#* '''1853''', Thomas de Quincey, "Autobiographical Sketches", ''Selections Grave and Gay'', Vol. I, p. 133:
#*: In Germany... a married couple, when celebrating the fiftieth anniversary of their marriage-day, are said to keep their [[golden jubilee]]; but on the twenty-fifth anniversary they have credit only for a '''silver jubilee'''.

